  "notes": "あんよ is baby talk (⟦{幼児語|ようじご}→幼児語：15843_youjigo⟧) for \"foot\" or \"walking.\" It comes from ⟦{足|あし}→足：00575_ashi⟧ (foot/leg) softened into a child-friendly form.\n\nUSAGE:\nFunctions as a noun (foot/leg) and a ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ verb (to walk).\n- あんよ⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{上手|じょうず}→上手：00707_jouzu⟧: good at walking (praise for toddlers)\n- あんよ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧/あんよ⟦できる→できる：00557_dekiru⟧: to walk (baby talk)\n- よちよちあんよ: toddling walk\n\nMILESTONE:\nOften used when discussing a baby's first steps — a key developmental milestone. Parents eagerly await when their child can あんよ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧.\n\nRELATED BABY TALK WORDS:\n- ⟦おてて→おてて：09104_otete⟧: hands (from ⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧)\n- ⟦おめめ→おめめ：09105_omeme⟧: eyes (from ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧)\n- ねん⟦ね→ね：09474_ne⟧: sleep (from ⟦{寝|ね}る→寝る：00470_neru⟧)\n- ⟦まんま→まんま：09108_manma⟧: food (from ごはん/まま)\n- おくち: mouth (from ⟦{口|くち}→口：00560_kuchi⟧)\n\nREGISTER:\nUsed only with babies and very small children. Using it with adults would be humorous or condescending.",
